# patch: 009-compact-signal
# depends: 002
# generated: 2026-08-21 (re-authored against 2.1.238)
# description: Emit a synthetic {type:"compact"} mirror event whenever the
#              session compacts its context, so a watching orchestrator is told
#              the worker may have DROPPED earlier context (its standing
#              task/charter) and can re-brief it. markPostCompaction()
#              (bootstrap/sessionState.js) is the single chokepoint every
#              compaction path funnels through -- full auto-compact and manual
#              /compact (both services/compact/compact.js) and the partial-
#              compaction runner (_unmatched/2840_Fdr.js) all call it exactly
#              once, right after the summary is in place and immediately before
#              reAppendSessionMetadataAfterCompaction(). Emitting here fires once
#              per real compaction with no duplication. Server routes it as a
#              "compact" notification to the worker's watchers (Router), queued +
#              delivered on the watcher's idle like other pings; it does NOT
#              touch the worker's idle flag (compaction happens mid-turn).
#
# UPSTREAM CHANGE 2.1.168 -> 2.1.238: the flat mutable STATE object is GONE.
#   Upstream split it into a composed root object of getters plus ~25
#   private-field class instances. Consequences for this patch:
#     - module moved: bootstrap/state.js -> bootstrap/sessionState.js
#       (bootstrap/state.js STILL EXISTS on 2.1.238 but is a DIFFERENT module --
#        OTel telemetry meters. Do not retarget this patch at it.)
#     - the body is no longer a field assignment. STATE.pendingPostCompaction = !0
#       became the accessor call
#       ROOT_SESSION.requestJournal.replacePendingPostCompaction(!0).
#   The chokepoint property was RE-VERIFIED on 2.1.238: still exactly three
#   callsites, still one call each, still immediately before
#   reAppendSessionMetadataAfterCompaction. Two of the three are now additionally
#   guarded on the querySource/agentContext check, which only narrows the emit to
#   compactions that actually persist post-compaction metadata -- the desired
#   semantics.
#
# CAVEAT (known, accept for v1): markPostCompaction has no agentId in scope, so
#   unlike turn_complete (query.js, guarded by !agentId) this also fires if a
#   SUBAGENT compacts -- read by the watcher as "the worker compacted". Harmless:
#   the watcher just holds a re-brief and reject-busy gates delivery. If it
#   proves noisy, move the emit to the three callsites and guard on the local
#   agentId var (compact.js t.agentId / r.agentId, 2840_Fdr.js d.agentId).
#
# All identifiers on ADDED lines are either anchored (none needed here) or
# claudiverse-owned (__claudiverse) -- no bundler-minified symbols are
# introduced. The two context lines pin the hunk to markPostCompaction's real
# body, so a rename drift fails loudly at --check.
diff --git a/bootstrap/sessionState.js b/bootstrap/sessionState.js
index 647ecbf..1759932 100644
--- a/bootstrap/sessionState.js
+++ b/bootstrap/sessionState.js
@@ -874,6 +874,9 @@ function setLastApiCompletionTimestamp(e) {
 
 function markPostCompaction() {
     ROOT_SESSION.requestJournal.replacePendingPostCompaction(!0);
+    try {
+        __claudiverse.mirrorMessage({ type: 'compact' });
+    } catch (e) {}
 }
 
 function consumePostCompaction() {
